  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Saute Onions - Set a large skillet over medium heat and add 2 Tbsp oil. Add onions and sauté until softened and golden, about 5 minutes."
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the chicken and sauté until the chicken is no longer pink on the outside, about 5 minutes. You don’t have to cook it through at this point."
    },
    {
      "text": "Build Flavor - Add minced garlic, ginger, cumin, coriander, garam masala, chili powder, turmeric, salt, pepper, and tomato paste. Cook for another 2 minutes, stirring constantly until the chicken is coated and the mixture is fragrant."
    },
    {
      "text": "Make the Sauce - Add yogurt, coconut cream, almond flour, and sugar and stir to combine. Bring to a light boil, then reduce the heat and simmer uncovered for 8-10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the chicken is cooked through and the sauce is reduced to your desired thickness."
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in the heavy cream and return to a simmer, then remove from heat. Season to taste with salt (I added an extra ¼ tsp salt)."
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve over white rice if desired and garnish with cilantro."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Notes*Do not shake the coconut milk can – this will make it easier to scoop off the rich cream portion at the top of the can for the sauce.",
